🧠 common_abilities/ – XI Shared System Utilities
This folder contains shared tools accessible by all XI agents (Davinci, Hermes, Sentinel). These tools cover memory validation, summary promotions, fuzzy scanning, vector control, and conflict resolution. Each script plays a role in the core maintenance, promotion, or semantic interaction with agent memory.

📜 Script Reference
✅ amend_memory_entry.py
Edits an existing memory entry by UUID.

Used to manually correct summaries, thoughts, or decisions.

Can update signature, written_by, or other metadata fields.

📌 append_summary_manifest.py
Appends new entries to the per-agent summary_manifest.json.

Updates include UUID, type (weekly/period/etc), file name, and timestamp.

Called after promotion to keep summary index current.

🧩 interactive_conflict_resolver.py
CLI tool for resolving memory conflicts across agent journals.

Supports side-by-side comparison and editing of contradictory entries.

Useful for human-guided debugging or arbitration of memory truth.

📥 load_summary_manifest.py
Loads the summary_manifest.json for any agent.

Returns parsed list of past summaries (with UUID, type, file path).

Utility helper for summary audits or GUI displays.

🔍 memory_fuzzy_scan.py
Scans memory files for similar or duplicate content using fuzzy logic.

Flags entries with high similarity scores for manual review.

Used by Sentinel and others for anomaly detection.

🧠 memory_index_daemon.py
Watches all agent memory folders.

Generates vector embeddings using local BERT-style encoder.

Feeds results into PostgreSQL pgvector table in real time.

Keeps track of indexed files with a hash snapshot log.

📥 memory_indexer.py
Standalone script to index new memory files into Postgres vector DB.

Similar to memory_index_daemon.py, but one-time or batch mode.

Used for full reindexing, catch-up runs, or after a config reset.

🔎 memory_search.py
Executes semantic search across indexed memory entries.

Supports top-k queries, date filtering, and agent/thread targeting.

Called by agents and vector controller.

🚨 raise_memory_conflict.py
Flags memory contradictions between agents or within the same agent.

Writes to disputed_entries.json for Sentinel review.

Logs details such as conflicting UUIDs, authors, and differences.

🧠 run_daily_summary_promotions.py
Automatically checks journal promotion thresholds for each agent.

Calls write_all_summaries_then_archive.py if thresholds are met.

Runs daily as part of background routine flow.

🕰️ time_utils.py
Defines 4-4-5 period structure used by XI (business-style calendar).

Includes get_current_quarter_and_period() and leap-year logic.

Used for journal tagging, archiving, and summary rotation.

🧪 validate_memory_file.py
Validates memory .json structure (uuid, summary, timestamp).

Supports single entry, list of entries, or entry bundles.

Reports any missing fields or malformed timestamps.

🧭 vector_controller.py
Parses and handles all sudo vector commands.

Tracks active agent sessions and vector quota limits.

Delegates actual search to memory_search.py.

📚 write_all_summaries_then_archive.py
Promotes memory from:

session → weekly

weekly → period

period → quarterly

Archives input entries after each successful promotion.

Adds fields like compiled_uuids, source_files, thoughts, and decisions.

Special logic for Sentinel audit flow.
